Southwest Kingdom, and the kingdom s02.","parentTitle":null}],"clan":{"id":"ac15-c9c4-c8fc","name":"Jinju Gang Clan","crest":"clan-crests/ac15-c9c4-c8fc.svg"},"generation":"opening","minors":false,"sourceKind":"proposal","locked":true,"values":{"Authority":-40,"Openness":20,"Force":-20,"Material":40,"Communal":40,"Principle":10,"Public":40,"Eligibility":70,"Dispersed":30,"Transformative":20},"desire":{"Longing":30,"Monopoly":-30,"Risk":10,"Display":-20,"Sustained":40,"Orientation":"Bisexual","Union":"Contract Cohabitation"},"fields":{"Affiliation":"Standards League","Livelihood":"Workshop Production Coordination","Rank":"Chairperson","Title":"Chair of the Standards League","Work Location":"Guro 5-dong. Gang Minseo lays the sealed crate of pump parts and the citizenship register side by side before the Guro 5-dong Guild Council. After sending back a deal that demands restoration-service registration in exchange, Gang Minseo hands Kim Nayul the shift roster of the workshops that refused, leaving it as grounds for the vote."},"sections":{"Life":"Generation of 2126. Raised in the Guro-Geumcheon industrial guild. The workshop elders taught by rejecting modifications made without standards. In the winter when the Eastern Agency demanded registration of restoration servants in exchange for parts, Gang Minseo placed the hand that refused registration onto the citizenship line. The workshop master chiefs made that line the basis for the chairmanship at the Guro Station Guild Council. If the Guard Corps subdues the workshops, the Standards League becomes a munitions factory. Daerim Lodging is a household within this realm. That is why Gang Minseo backs Baek On''s register.","Offices":"Rank: Chairman. Title: Chairman of the Standards League. Occupational alias: Fabrication Council Arbiter.","Anecdote":"When the Eastern Agency held out a register of restoration servants instead of a crate of pump parts, Gang Minseo sent the crate back sealed. That seal remained as a debt between Han Jaemok''s Western Water Supply and Bae Ujin''s Ministry of War.","Houses":"House of Guro Alloy (HC07). Steward. The standards drawing cabinet is this house''s key.","Relationships":"Supplies pump parts to Han Jaemok. Disputes the scope of technology disclosure with Jeong Hojun. Supports Baek On''s refugee citizenship.\n\n- Affiliation: Standards League\n- Occupation: Workshop fabrication coordination\n- Rank: Chairman\n- Title: Chairman of the Standards League\n- Work location: Guro 5-dong. Gang Minseo lays the sealed crate of pump parts and the citizenship register side by side before the Guro 5-dong Guild Council. After sending back a deal that demands restoration-service registration in exchange, Gang Minseo hands Kim Nayul the shift roster of the workshops that refused, leaving it as grounds for the vote."},"biography":"**Life.** Generation of 2126. Raised in the Guro-Geumcheon industrial guild. The workshop elders taught by rejecting modifications made without standards. In the winter when the Eastern Agency demanded registration of restoration servants in exchange for parts, Gang Minseo placed the hand that refused registration onto the citizenship line. The workshop master chiefs made that line the basis for the chairmanship at the Guro Station Guild Council. If the Guard Corps subdues the workshops, the Standards League becomes a munitions factory. Daerim Lodging is a household within this realm. That is why Gang Minseo backs Baek On''s register.\n**Office.** Rank: Chairman. Title: Chairman of the Standards League. Occupational alias: Fabrication Council Arbiter.\n**Anecdote.** When the Eastern Agency held out a register of restoration servants instead of a crate of pump parts, Gang Minseo sent the crate back sealed. That seal remained as a debt between Han Jaemok''s Western Water Supply and Bae Ujin''s Ministry of War.\n**House.** House of Guro Alloy (HC07). Steward. The standards drawing cabinet is this house''s key.\n**Relations.** Supplies pump parts to Han Jaemok. Disputes the scope of technology disclosure with Jeong Hojun. Supports Baek On''s refugee citizenship.\n\n- Affiliation: Standards League\n- Occupation: Workshop fabrication coordination\n- Rank: Chairman\n- Title: Chairman of the Standards League\n- Work location: Guro 5-dong. Gang Minseo lays the sealed crate of pump parts and the citizenship register side by side before the Guro 5-dong Guild Council. After sending back a deal that demands restoration-service registration in exchange, Gang Minseo hands Kim Nayul the shift roster of the workshops that refused, leaving it as grounds for the vote.","relations":{"outgoing":[],"incoming":[{"from":"Choe Han-gyeol","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Pump and wheel parts supply contract"},{"from":"Jeong Siu","type":"Master and Disciple","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Learns fabrication standards under the Arbiter as a pupil"},{"from":"Kim Nayul","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Enforces exchange designs at the guild worksite"},{"from":"I Gangmuk","type":"Rivalry","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Contests the munitions monopoly and arbitration authority"},{"from":"Bak Soeon","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Backs the process division at the building guild"},{"from":"Bak Hayul","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Receives needed parts to southwest standards"},{"from":"Sin Boram","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Supports citizenship solidarity at the family council"},{"from":"Yun Choa","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Consults the restoration-service citizenship text"},{"from":"Jo U-chan","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Applies repair standards to the work crew"},{"from":"Yeo Sion","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Posting Gang Minseo''s Standards League council declaration in the Guro alleys"},{"from":"Ran Min-jun","type":"Contract","to":"Gang Minseo","basis":"Consulting Gang Minseo''s text on voluntary adult restora