n:1135062100","region:1135062400","region:1135062500","region:1135063000","region:1135064000","region:1135066500","region:1135067000","region:1135069500","region:1135070000","region:1135071000","region:1135072000","region:1138051000","region:1138052000","region:1138053000","region:1138055100","region:1138055200","region:1138056000","region:1138057000","region:1138058000","region:1138059000","region:1138060000","region:1138062500","region:1138063100","region:1138063200","region:1138064000","region:1138065000","region:1138069000","region:1141052000","region:1141055500","region:1141056500","region:1141065500","region:1141066000","region:1141068500","region:1165051000","region:1165053000","region:1165053100","region:1174051500","region:1174052500","region:1174052600","region:1174053000","region:1174054000","region:1174055000","region:1174056000","region:1174057000","region:1174058000","region:1174059000","region:1174060000","region:1174061000","region:1174062000","region:1174064000","region:1174065000","region:1174066000","region:1174068500","region:1174069000","region:1174070000"],"basis":"Opening Kingdom Route Decision (User Approval 2026-10-11)","parentTitle":null},{"id":"title:kingdom-geography:seoul:01","name":"Central Kingdom","rank":"kingdom","holderPersonId":"K144","stateId":"S06","geographicTitleId":"geography:kingdom:seoul:01","basis":"Territorial Title Distribution of 2026-10-22 (owner:seoul-faction-consolidation-20261022). President of the Republic of Korea. Basis for holding the northern Gangbuk region centered on Cheongwadae and Gwanghwamun, and the Jongno Duchy.","parentTitle":null}],"clan":{"id":"c724-d30c-d3c9","name":"Papyeong Yun Clan","crest":"clan-crests/c724-d30c-d3c9.svg"},"generation":"opening","minors":false,"sourceKind":"proposal","locked":true,"values":{"Authority":20,"Openness":-10,"Force":-30,"Material":-20,"Communal":10,"Principle":40,"Public":-30,"Eligibility":0,"Dispersed":-40,"Transformative":-50},"desire":{"Longing":-10,"Monopoly":10,"Risk":-40,"Display":-20,"Sustained":40,"Orientation":"None","Union":"None"},"fields":{"Livelihood":"Seal Box Sealing and Ratification Hold Management","Constitutional Body":"President of the Republic of Korea","Offices":"President of the Republic of Korea"},"sections":{"Life":"Yun Seorin handled records while serving registry duty at the Government Complex Seoul main building, 209 Sejong-daero, Jongno-gu. Forging records is forbidden. Without the government seal, water-supply contracts in the city center are invalid. Yun Seorin became president after keeping the seal chest of the Bukhansan Bogungmun Records House unbroken. The seal chest of the Seoul Station Records Law House belongs to Yeo Rian. In 2126 the government handles the residents'' register and the rationing and ratification affairs of Jongno and Jung-gu from Cheongwadae, while the Government Complex Seoul guard corps protects the downtown stations. If Han Jaemok''s western proposal is halted, debts pile up; if it is stamped, Yangcheon''s veto dies.","Offices":"Rank: President. Office: President of the Republic of Korea. Occupational alias: Records Bureau Chief (separate from the presidential post).","Anecdote":"When three wills were received, Yun Seorin put ratification on hold and only verified the seal on the chest.","Houses":"Bukhansan Bogungmun Records House (HC05). Custodian. The custodian of the Seoul Station Records Law House (HP04) is Yeo Rian.","Relationships":"Dispute over ratification authority with Han Jaemok. Rationing ledger exchange with Nam Yungyeong. Ratification rivalry with Jeong Yura.\n\n- Occupation: Seal chest sealing and ratification hold management\n- Constitutional body: President of the Republic of Korea\n- Constitutional body: President of the Republic of Korea\n- Office: President of the Republic of Korea\n- Yun Seorin''s registry duty at the Government Complex Seoul and management of seal chest sealing and ratification holds are tied to the work of Sajik-dong.\n- Yun Seorin''s handling of the Jongno and Jung-gu residents'' register and the rationing and ratification affairs at Cheongwadae is tied to Cheongun-hyoja-dong.\n- Yun Seorin''s care of the seal chest of the Bukhansan Bogungmun Records House is tied to the work of Jeongneung 4-dong.\n\nThe true power broker who actually runs the ratification, notarization, map and medical-transfer ledgers beside Records Bureau Chief Yun Seorin."},"biography":"**Life.** Yun Seorin handled records while serving registry duty at the Government Complex Seoul main building, 209 Sejong-daero, Jongno-gu. Forging records is forbidden. Without the government seal, water-supply contracts in the city center are invalid. Yun Seorin became president after keeping the seal chest of the Bukhansan Bogungmun Records House unbroken. The seal chest of the Seoul Station Records Law House belongs to Yeo Rian. In 2126 the government handles the residents'' register and the rationing and ratification affairs of Jongno and Jung-gu from Cheongwadae, while the Government Complex Seoul guard corps protects the downtown stations. If Han Jaemok''s western proposal is halted, debts pile up; if it is stamped, Yangcheon''s veto dies.\n**Office.** Rank: President. Office: President of the Republic of Korea. Occupational alias: Records Bureau Chief (separate from the presidential post).\n**Anecdote.** When three wills were received, Yun Seorin put ratification on hold and only verified the seal on the chest.\n**House.** Bukhansan Bogungmun Records House (HC05). Custodian. The custodian of the Seoul Station Records Law House (HP04) is Yeo Rian.\n**Relations.** Dispute over ratification authority with Han Jaemok. Rationing ledger exchange with Nam Yungyeong. Ratification rivalry with Jeong Yura.\n\n- Occupation: Seal chest sealing and ratification hold management\n- Constitutional body: President of the Republic of Korea\n- Constitutional body: President of the Republic of Korea\n- Office: President of the Republic of Korea\n- Yun Seorin''s registry duty at the Government Complex Seoul and management of seal chest sealing and ratification holds are tied to the work of Sajik-dong.\n- Yun Seorin''s handling of the Jongno and Jung-gu residents'' register and the rationing and ratification affairs at Cheongwadae is tied to Cheongun-hyoja-dong.\n- Yun Seorin''s care of the seal chest of the Bukhansan Bogungmun Records House is tied to the work of Jeongneung 4-dong.\n\nThe true power broker who actually runs the ratification, notarization, map and medical-transfer ledgers beside Records Bureau Chief Yun Seorin.","relations":{"outgoing":[],"incoming":[{"from":"Kim Yeongyu","type":"Contract","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Registration of Onmin''s Documents"},{"from":"Kim Yeongyu","type":"Rivalry","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Registration of Onmin''s documents is permitted, but ratification is denied"},{"from":"O Gyeongjae","type":"Rivalry","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Checks the president''s ratification authority by disclosing the three wills"},{"from":"Jeong Gaon","type":"Contract","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Handed the will copies over to the Records Office"},{"from":"Gang Ye-jun","type":"Command","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Reviews the ratification of the Session Chair under the President''s command"},{"from":"Jo Ha-rin","type":"Command","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Guards the three copies of Im Hajun''s will in the archive"},{"from":"Yun Ji-yul","type":"Command","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Medical Transfer Records of the Presidential Backers"},{"from":"O Seo-yul","type":"Command","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Reviewing the water-supply drafts under delegated notarial authority"},{"from":"Jeon Nagyeong","type":"Contract","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Handing a copy of the ration ledger over to the Records Office"},{"from":"Jang Pil-gyu","type":"Rivalry","to":"Yun Seo-rin","basis":"Rivalry over interpretive authority of the ratified water supply contract copy"},{"from":"Na Bomgyeol","type":"Contract","to":"